## Metadata
Author: T. W. Martin, Jr.
Copyright: New York World
Date: 1914-08-02
Number: 30
Description: A zigzag W of 3-wide stepped bands, 8 rows by 31 columns: two peaks of three squares in the top row, a valley of three in the middle of the bottom row, and three-square ends at bottom left and bottom right; every word is two or three letters.
Source: Milwaukee Sentinel, 1914-08-02, p. 69
Solution-Source: Milwaukee Sentinel, 1914-08-09, p. 75


## Printed
heading: FUN'S CROSS-WORD PUZZLE
number: No 30.
credit: FUN'S cross word puzzle No. 30 was designed by T. W. Martin, Jr., of Baltimore, Md. This puzzle in FUN'S series may truthfully be called the young folks' number. As will be readily seen, it contains only one syllable words.
instructions: The following clews will aid you in correctly solving the puzzle. Work it out yourself and then see how your solution compares with that which will be published in next week's issue of FUN.
solution heading: Solution to Last Week's Cross-Word Puzzle.


